# ⚠ THE CRLF FLIP-FLOP, ENDED.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` on this machine with no `.gitattributes` meant git-written
# files landed CRLF and agent-written ones landed LF. Two suites once went red for
# that reason alone while the shipped code was correct, and the next branch switch
# could always redden a different one. That is a whole debugging session spent on
# an instrument rather than on the game.
#
# Normalising the TEXT formats to LF in the repo makes the working tree
# deterministic regardless of who or what wrote a file. Godot reads LF happily on
# Windows; so does Python.
*.gd     text eol=lf
*.gdshader text eol=lf
*.tres   text eol=lf
*.tscn   text eol=lf
*.godot  text eol=lf
*.cfg    text eol=lf
*.uid    text eol=lf
*.py     text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf

# Binary — never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.wav binary
*.ogg binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary

# cmd.exe is not reliable on LF-only line endings, and `goto :label` across a
# mangled file is exactly how the last batch wrapper died. Force CRLF on
# checkout so a clone on any machine gets a file cmd.exe can actually read.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
# PowerShell is happy either way, but keep it consistent with what Windows
# tooling writes so the file does not churn on every edit.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Web files are deployed as-is to a Linux edge and parsed there. `_headers` in
# particular is read by Cloudflare's own parser, so pin LF rather than let this
# machine's autocrlf hand a fresh clone CRLF versions of files that leave it.
site/_headers text eol=lf
site/robots.txt text eol=lf
site/sitemap.xml text eol=lf
site/index.html text eol=lf
site/404.html text eol=lf
site/llms.txt text eol=lf
